LICENSING
=========

This repository is released under two licences, because it contains two
different kinds of work.

1. THE WRITTEN WORK AND THE FIGURES
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

   Covers: report/, figures/*.png, figures/notes/, docs/, README.md, and the
   cleaning rule files and validation logs under data/*/rules/ and data/*/logs/.

   You may share and adapt this material, including commercially, provided
   you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and state whether you
   made changes.

   Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
   Summary:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Please cite as:
   Ilo, C.O. (2026) UK Packaging Recovery Evidence, 2023 to 2026:
   What the published data shows, and what it cannot. Nova Cyclos.

2. THE CODE
   MIT Licence. See LICENSE-CODE-MIT.txt.

   Covers: data/*/scripts/, data/*/run_all.sh, and figures/build/.

3. THE UNDERLYING DATA
   The files under data/*/raw/ are not mine. They are published by UK public
   bodies and remain subject to the terms of their original publishers, which
   for most UK government data is the Open Government Licence v3.0.
   https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

